|YKOThe Center of Town is Darkwind City's main crossroads. If a new
character becomes lost, |YKBncot|YKO returns there. Pull the dispenser lever
at the crossroads whenever you need another Newbie Tome.

Erga's newbie store, four west and one south of the Center of Town, gives
free equipment to characters through level 5. The donation room, five north
and one east, holds equipment donated by veterans. Use |YKBget|YKO,
|YKBwear|YKO, |YKBwield|YKO, and |YKBequip|YKO, then check the result with
|YKBeq|YKO or |YKBmyeq|YKO.

The newbie farm is a safe place to practice looking, moving, fighting, and
healing. Death has no penalty through level 5. Above level 5 it costs only
10 percent of the experience you currently hold: no stats or levels are
lost, and your corpse travels safely with you to the church.

Level at the Adventurers' Guild with |YKBadvance|YKO. You can inspect stat
costs from anywhere with |YKBremcost|YKO and buy normal advancement with
|YKBremadvance <stat>|YKO or |YKBremadvance level|YKO. Guild advancement
still follows the rules of the guild you choose. Non-remort characters may
use |YKBset autolevel on|YKO, but leaving it off lets you bank experience
for stat raises.

Qualifying carried and equipped gear now saves when you leave the game.
Donated, broken, unique, consumable, non-droppable, and specially restricted
items may not save; items inside containers do not save merely because the
container does. Chapter 7 explains equipment in more detail.|000

